# Backend quality
- Determine framework and runtime versions from project files before writing code.
- Separate routing, request validation, application services, persistence and transport representations.
- Return deliberate status codes, safe error messages, structured logs and consistent API response shapes.
- Enforce authorization at the service/resource level, not only by hiding UI controls.
- Use database transactions for atomic multi-step writes and define concurrency/idempotency behavior.
- Avoid N+1 queries; use bounded pagination and appropriate indexes.
- For Laravel use migrations, FormRequest, policies/gates, queues/events where appropriate and PHPUnit/Pest.
- For Node prefer TypeScript, explicit schemas (e.g. Zod) and controlled async error propagation.
- Write unit and integration tests for happy path, invalid inputs, unauthorized requests and conflicts.
